# HWPX XML structure: header/section relationships and ID references
`references/hwpx-format.md` supplies **values**: HWPUNIT, A4 dimensions, namespaces.
This document supplies **structure**: required parent/child relationships and what
Hancom does when those relationships are wrong.
The failures here were extracted from **actual Hancom rejections**, not inferred
from a schema. They describe concrete failure behavior rather than theoretical expectations.
---
## 1. File responsibilities: header defines, section references
| File | Contains | Does not contain |
|---|---|---|
| `Contents/header.xml` | **Definitions** of fonts, character/paragraph properties, border fills, styles, numbering | Body text |
| `Contents/section0.xml` | Paragraphs, tables, objects, and **references** to definitions | Formatting definitions |
This boundary is **strict**. Sections have no place for inline formatting definitions.
Create an `<hh:paraPr>` in the header, then reference its `id` from the section's
`paraPrIDRef`.
### Five ID-reference pairs
| Referencing attribute | Header definition | Definition container |
|---|---|---|
| `hp:p/@paraPrIDRef` | `hh:paraPr/@id` | `hh:paraProperties` |
| `hp:p/@styleIDRef` | `hh:style/@id` | `hh:styles` |
| `hp:run/@charPrIDRef` | `hh:charPr/@id` | `hh:charProperties` |
| `hp:tbl/@borderFillIDRef`, `hp:cellzone`, `hp:tc/hp:cellBorderFill/@borderFillIDRef` | `hh:borderFill/@id` | `hh:borderFills` |
| `hh:charPr/@borderFillIDRef` (within the header) | `hh:borderFill/@id` | `hh:borderFills` |
**All IDRef values are compared as strings.** `"01"` and `"1"` differ.
`validate_hwpx.py --semantic` checks this through `reference/undefined`.
**Each container has an independent ID namespace.** `charPr id="2"` and
`borderFill id="2"` are unrelated. Missing this distinction makes unexpected boxes
around every character difficult to diagnose. See `scripts/fix_borders.py` and §5.
**`itemCnt` is functional metadata.** `<hh:charProperties itemCnt="7">` must match
the child count. Adding entries without updating it makes Hancom silently discard
later items, often delaying detection because no error dialog appears.
---
## 2. `hp:secPr`: misplaced attributes trigger a corruption dialog
**This is the most costly failure.** Generators often express page settings like this:
```xml
<!-- Incorrect: Hancom displays a "파일이 손상되었습니다" corruption dialog -->
<hp:secPr pageWidth="59528" pageHeight="84186"
leftMargin="8504" rightMargin="8504" topMargin="5668"/>
```
`pageWidth`, `pageHeight`, `leftMargin`, `rightMargin`, `topMargin`, and
`bottomMargin` **are not `hp:secPr` attributes**. OWPML defines no such attributes;
Hancom treats the entire secPr as unreadable rather than ignoring them.
The actual schema nests **`hp:margin` inside an `hp:pagePr` child**.
Actual content from `templates/base/Contents/section0.xml`:
```xml
<hp:secPr id="" textDirection="HORIZONTAL" spaceColumns="1134"
tabStop="8000" tabStopVal="4000" tabStopUnit="HWPUNIT"
outlineShapeIDRef="1" memoShapeIDRef="0"
textVerticalWidthHead="0" masterPageCnt="0">
<hp:grid lineGrid="0" charGrid="0" wonggojiFormat="0"/>
<hp:startNum pageStartsOn="BOTH" page="0" pic="0" tbl="0" equation="0"/>
<hp:visibility hideFirstHeader="0" hideFirstFooter="0" .../>
<hp:lineNumberShape restartType="0" countBy="0" distance="0" startNumber="0"/>
<hp:pagePr landscape="WIDELY" width="59528" height="84186" gutterType="LEFT_ONLY">
<hp:margin header="4252" footer="4252" gutter="0"
left="8504" right="8504" top="5668" bottom="4252"/>
</hp:pagePr>
<hp:footNotePr>…</hp:footNotePr>
<hp:endNotePr>…</hp:endNotePr>
<hp:pageBorderFill type="BOTH" borderFillIDRef="1" .../>
</hp:secPr>
```
Margin names are `left`, `right`, `top`, and `bottom`, not `leftMargin`.
The same element also contains `header`, `footer`, and `gutter`.
### secPr placement contract
Place `hp:secPr` **inside the first `hp:run` of section0.xml's first paragraph**.
Outside that paragraph or in the second paragraph, it causes Hancom to lose section
settings. `hp:colPr` belongs in the same location as its companion.
`validate_hwpx.py --semantic` checks this with `document/structure`, reporting
`first paragraph is missing hp:secPr`. The same check covers **child completeness**:
all six required children above must exist. An incomplete secPr may still open,
but page size and margins revert to Hancom defaults and invalidate procurement formatting.
---
## 3. `hp:pic`: missing required children can crash Hancom
Pictures can **crash Hancom itself**, without a dialog or log, instead of merely
preventing a file from opening. The required children are therefore listed in full.
```xml
<hp:pic reverse="0">
<!-- 1. Shared ShapeComponent fields: fixed order -->
<hp:offset x="0" y="0"/>
<hp:orgSz width="30000" height="20000"/>
<hp:curSz width="30000" height="20000"/>
<hp:flip horizontal="0" vertical="0"/>
<hp:rotationInfo angle="0" centerX="15000" centerY="10000" rotateimage="1"/>
<hp:renderingInfo>
<hc:transMatrix e1="1" e2="0" e3="0" e4="0" e5="1" e6="0"/>
<hc:scaMatrix e1="1" e2="0" e3="0" e4="0" e5="1" e6="0"/>
<hc:rotMatrix e1="1" e2="0" e3="0" e4="0" e5="1" e6="0"/>
</hp:renderingInfo>
<!-- 2. Placement -->
<hp:sz width="30000" widthRelTo="ABSOLUTE"
height="20000" heightRelTo="ABSOLUTE" protect="0"/>
<hp:pos treatAsChar="1" affectLSpacing="0" flowWithText="1" allowOverlap="0"
holdAnchorAndSO="0" vertRelTo="PARA" horzRelTo="COLUMN"
vertAlign="TOP" horzAlign="LEFT" vertOffset="0" horzOffset="0"/>
<hp:outMargin left="0" right="0" top="0" bottom="0"/>
<!-- 3. Picture-specific fields -->
<hp:lineShape color="#000000" width="0" style="NONE" endCap="FLAT"
headStyle="NORMAL" tailStyle="NORMAL"
headfill="1" tailfill="1" headSz="MEDIUM" tailSz="MEDIUM"
outlineStyle="NORMAL" alpha="0"/>
<hp:imgRect>
<hc:pt0 x="0" y="0"/>
<hc:pt1 x="30000" y="0"/>
<hc:pt2 x="30000" y="20000"/>
<hc:pt3 x="0" y="20000"/>
</hp:imgRect>
<hp:imgClip left="0" right="30000" top="0" bottom="20000"/>
<hp:inMargin left="0" right="0" top="0" bottom="0"/>
<hp:imgDim dimwidth="30000" dimheight="20000"/>
<hc:img binaryItemIDRef="image1" bright="0" contrast="0"
effect="REAL_PIC" alpha="0.0"/>
</hp:pic>
```
**Four frequent omissions account for most crashes:**
1. All four vertices `hc:pt0` through `hc:pt3` under `hp:imgRect`; three are insufficient.
2. `hp:imgClip`, set to the **full image area** even without cropping.
3. `hp:imgDim`, even if its values match `curSz`.
4. All three matrices under `hp:renderingInfo`; none may be omitted.
### Register pictures in three places
Correct picture XML without registered binary data opens as an empty rectangle.
| Location | Entry |
|---|---|
| `BinData/image1.png` | Actual image bytes |
| `<opf:manifest>` in `Contents/content.hpf` | `<opf:item id="image1" href="BinData/image1.png" media-type="image/png"/>` |
| `META-INF/manifest.xml` | An `<odf:file-entry>` for the same path |
`hc:img/@binaryItemIDRef` references the **manifest `id`, not a file path**.
Using a path produces an empty picture without an error.
---
## 4. `hh:paraPr`: alignment and margins are children too
Paragraph properties have the same attribute-versus-child trap as secPr.
```xml
<!-- Incorrect: no error, but the entire style is ignored -->
<hh:paraPr id="1" align="JUSTIFY" indent="0" left="0" right="0"/>
```
Hancom renders this with **default paragraph properties**. The silent failure appears
as formatting that does not apply. The actual structure uses children:
```xml
<hh:paraPr id="1" tabPrIDRef="0" condense="0" fontLineHeight="0"
snapToGrid="1" suppressLineNumbers="0" checked="0">
<hh:align horizontal="JUSTIFY" vertical="BASELINE"/>
<hh:heading type="NONE" idRef="0" level="0"/>
<hh:breakSetting breakLatinWord="KEEP_WORD" breakNonLatinWord="KEEP_WORD"
widowOrphan="0" keepWithNext="0" keepLines="0"
pageBreakBefore="0" lineWrap="BREAK"/>
<hh:margin>
<hc:intent value="0" unit="HWPUNIT"/>
<hc:left value="0" unit="HWPUNIT"/>
<hc:right value="0" unit="HWPUNIT"/>
<hc:prev value="0" unit="HWPUNIT"/>
<hc:next value="0" unit="HWPUNIT"/>
</hh:margin>
<hh:lineSpacing type="PERCENT" value="160" unit="HWPUNIT"/>
<hh:border borderFillIDRef="2" offsetLeft="0" offsetRight="0"
offsetTop="0" offsetBottom="0" connect="0" ignoreMargin="0"/>
</hh:paraPr>
```
Margins are **child elements carrying `value` and `unit`**, not numeric attributes.
Hancom-generated files may wrap this block in `hp:switch` / `hp:case` for version
branching. Finding `hh:margin` then requires descending through that wrapper.
Use **descendant searches** such as `findall(".//hh:margin")` rather than only direct children.
---
## 5. Order for header edits
Editing the section before its header creates a broken intermediate file. Use this order:
1. **Add the definition** to the header and update `itemCnt`.
2. **Reference its `id`** from the section.
3. Run `validate_hwpx.py --semantic` and require zero `reference/undefined` findings.
4. For **deletion**, reverse the order: remove references before removing definitions.
Deleting definitions first makes every intermediate validation fail, obscuring actual
defects. This is why the five-stage repair sequence in `references/validation-rules.md`
places `delete` last and requires evidence.
---
